<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγγᾰλ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>intricate knot</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				48
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμεῖς . . ἀεὶ στραγγαλίδας
				ἐσφίγγετε</span> tied <i>knots</i> fast (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγγαλιάω</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				21
			</span></i>: hence Aristocreon called Chrysippus <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Ἀκαδημιακῶν στραγγαλίδων κοπίδα</span>, a knife to
			cut Academic <i>knots</i>, ap.<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1033e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>knot</i> or <i>induration</i> in the breast or other parts,
				<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				587b22
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγγαλιά</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> some kind of ornament,
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jd.</u>
				8.26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀργυρᾶ, ς. χρυσᾶ
			κεκολλημένη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1449.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
